* gf180mcu PMOS pass-device Rds(on) / dropout characterization
* Issue #4 - template; fets/run.sh substitutes @TOKENS@ and runs the deck.
*
* Topology: source and bulk at Vin, gate at 0 V (the best drive a
* ground-referenced error amp can deliver, so Vsg = Vin - no idealized
* overdrive), drain is the regulator output node. Two measurements per (W,L):
*   1. forced-load-current dropout : ideal Iload sink on the drain, Vsd measured
*   2. linear-region on-resistance : drain held 50 mV below source, Id measured
* Unit cell is w=100u / nf=10 (10 um per finger); total W = 100u * m.
* vd_v is the raw drain node voltage: vd_v <= 0 means the device cannot
* source the load current at all at this corner (infeasible, not a dropout).
*
.include @MODELS@/design.ngspice
.lib @MODELS@/sm141064.ngspice @CORNER@
.options temp=@TEMP@
.param vin=@VIN@

vin vin 0 dc 'vin'
vg  g   0 dc 0

x1 d1 g vin vin @DEV@ w=100u l=@L1@ nf=10 m=10
i1 d1 0 dc 50m
x2 d2 g vin vin @DEV@ w=100u l=@L1@ nf=10 m=10
i2 d2 0 dc 100m
x3 d3 g vin vin @DEV@ w=100u l=@L1@ nf=10 m=10
v3 d3 0 dc 'vin-0.05'
x4 d4 g vin vin @DEV@ w=100u l=@L1@ nf=10 m=20
i4 d4 0 dc 50m
x5 d5 g vin vin @DEV@ w=100u l=@L1@ nf=10 m=20
i5 d5 0 dc 100m
